WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.795
♪ <i>It seems today that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.796 --> 00:08.174
♪ <i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:08.175 --> 00:11.886
♪ <i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.887 --> 00:14.847
♪ <i>On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.848 --> 00:18.142
♪ <i>Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.143 --> 00:21.604
♪ <i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.605 --> 00:23.064
♪ <i>All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.065 --> 00:24.690
♪ <i>Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.691 --> 00:30.155
♪ <i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:34.076 --> 00:36.327
All right. Empty school.

00:36.328 --> 00:39.288
Time to<i> Shining</i> my way
through the halls.

00:50.926 --> 00:53.928
Principal Shepherd, where is everyone?!

00:53.929 --> 00:57.056
Principal Shepherd's not here,

00:57.057 --> 00:59.016
Miss Griffin.

00:59.017 --> 01:00.685
Why are you talking like that?

01:00.686 --> 01:02.019
Sorry. That was Tony,

01:02.020 --> 01:03.521
the little boy who lives in my mouth.

01:03.522 --> 01:04.939
Why are you here? It's skip day.

01:04.940 --> 01:07.233
It's skip day? Nobody told me.

01:07.234 --> 01:10.875
She's unpopular and unattractive.

01:10.876 --> 01:12.573
Tony!

01:17.077 --> 01:20.204
Hello?! Chris?

01:20.205 --> 01:22.540
Did you know it was skip day?

01:22.541 --> 01:24.835
Mom? Dad?

01:30.591 --> 01:32.375
Hello?

01:32.376 --> 01:34.802
<i>- Mom? Where are you guys?</i>
- Who is this?

01:34.803 --> 01:37.061
<i>It's Meg. Where is everyone?</i>

01:37.062 --> 01:39.748
Well, this can't be Meg.
She's with us here at the pier.

01:39.749 --> 01:41.888
- Who is that?
- Someone who says she's Meg.

01:41.889 --> 01:42.895
Give me that.

01:42.896 --> 01:46.105
Okay,<i> Meg,</i> if this is you,
what's your birthday?

01:46.106 --> 01:47.565
<i>March 23.</i>

01:47.566 --> 01:49.400
I have no idea if that's correct.

01:49.401 --> 01:50.860
Good day, sir.

01:50.861 --> 01:52.653
Sorry about that, everyone.

01:52.654 --> 01:56.116
Now let's get back to the fair
and enjoy our March 23.

02:08.170 --> 02:10.129
The usual, please.

02:10.130 --> 02:12.256
Here ya are...
Ladies' seven on the left,

02:12.257 --> 02:13.838
and men's 11 on the right.

02:13.839 --> 02:15.426
I just need a license.

02:15.427 --> 02:17.136
Thanks.

02:17.137 --> 02:19.848
Oh! And happy birthday!

02:32.444 --> 02:33.820
Yes!

02:44.790 --> 02:47.959
We have not updated those.

02:51.588 --> 02:53.172
<i>Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.</i>

02:53.173 --> 02:55.299
<i>Coming up, I find even more sand</i>

02:55.300 --> 02:58.552
<i>on my body from a beach toilet
I used a week ago.</i>

02:58.553 --> 03:01.138
<i>But first,
tragedy strikes close to home,</i>

03:01.139 --> 03:03.516
<i>as a car crash near
my apartment claims the life</i>

03:03.517 --> 03:05.059
<i>of a local teen girl.</i>

03:05.060 --> 03:06.977
<i>The victim's identity is being withheld</i>

03:06.978 --> 03:08.938
<i>pending notification of the family.</i>

03:11.024 --> 03:12.900
Hey, buddy.

03:12.901 --> 03:15.695
What brings you around at this
late hour with your uniform on

03:15.696 --> 03:18.155
and your hat held mournfully
against your chest?

03:18.156 --> 03:21.742
Peter, Lois, it pains me above the waist

03:21.743 --> 03:23.411
to tell you that Meg is dead.

03:23.412 --> 03:24.995
- What?!
- What are you talking about?

03:24.996 --> 03:26.205
Meg's right here.

03:29.695 --> 03:32.360
You know, it's weird that didn't
happen on the pier all day.

03:32.361 --> 03:34.338
Or when we rented that convertible.

03:34.339 --> 03:35.923
How did this happen?!

03:35.924 --> 03:38.509
She got in a car wreck, and
was burned beyond recognition,

03:38.510 --> 03:41.095
and I leveled up on Fortnite
this weekend,

03:41.096 --> 03:43.681
but you probably only care
about the first two things.

03:43.682 --> 03:46.035
Oh, dear God, no!

03:46.036 --> 03:49.230
All we found was Meg's
driver's license at the scene.

03:51.606 --> 03:54.942
It had her Quiznos punch card
stuck to the back.

03:54.943 --> 03:58.237
Your little angel was
one stamp away from a free sub,

03:58.238 --> 04:00.990
which only adds
to this horrific tragedy.

04:00.991 --> 04:02.366
It's actually pretty impressive,

04:02.367 --> 04:05.619
because the card was only issued
three days ago.

04:05.620 --> 04:08.247
Usually one of the guys would
swipe a thing like this,

04:08.248 --> 04:10.916
use it on the way home,
but I snagged it for ya.

04:10.917 --> 04:13.085
Thought Meg's family ought
to be the ones

04:13.086 --> 04:15.045
to enjoy the free sandwich.

04:15.046 --> 04:17.840
Again, I'm very sorry.

04:21.720 --> 04:23.137
<i>Oh, hang on.</i>

04:23.138 --> 04:24.972
<i>Oh, they told the family? Great!</i>

04:24.973 --> 04:27.850
<i>The girl killed near
my apartment was Meg Griffin.</i>

04:27.851 --> 04:29.894
What? I'm not dead!

04:29.895 --> 04:31.729
<i>She was burned beyond recognition</i>

04:31.730 --> 04:33.731
<i>but identified by her driver's license.</i>

04:33.732 --> 04:35.816
<i>156 pounds.</i>

04:35.817 --> 04:37.235
<i>Yikes.</i>

04:37.236 --> 04:40.237
Wait. Did you give my ID
to the wrong girl?

04:40.238 --> 04:44.242
Sorry. Them shoe spray fumes
made me all goofy in my head.

04:47.078 --> 04:49.897
I'm still sober. This ain't cheatin'!

04:49.898 --> 04:51.916
Oh, this is me being sober!

04:53.502 --> 04:55.419
So I guess I'm dead.

04:55.420 --> 04:57.589
And no one cares.

04:59.633 --> 05:01.133
<i>Again, for those of you</i>

05:01.134 --> 05:03.220
<i>in a new scene: Meg Griffin dead.</i>

05:40.507 --> 05:43.013
Lois, can you believe these seats?

05:43.014 --> 05:44.343
Front row!

05:44.344 --> 05:47.346
I hope the priest pulls me up
on stage and dances with me.

05:47.347 --> 05:50.683
When I was hastily relocated
to this parish a week ago,

05:50.684 --> 05:52.893
the last thing
I thought I'd have to do is

05:52.894 --> 05:55.813
stand before you on such a sad occasion.

05:55.814 --> 05:57.398
A family losing a child is like

05:57.399 --> 05:59.900
a Trivial Pursuit wheel
losing a pie piece.

05:59.901 --> 06:02.862
And you have to keep reminding
everyone playing the game,

06:02.863 --> 06:06.156
"Don't forget. I already got
'Entertainment'." What a pain.

06:06.157 --> 06:09.202
Your first speaker...
Principal Shepherd.

06:10.412 --> 06:12.830
Meg Griffin was an honest man,

06:12.831 --> 06:15.207
a kind man, a man who knew how...

06:16.537 --> 06:18.002
Oh, my stars!

06:18.003 --> 06:20.004
I have nothing.

06:20.005 --> 06:21.922
Kind of feel bad. There's nobody here.

06:21.923 --> 06:23.841
I know.<i> We're</i> not even here.

06:27.012 --> 06:28.888
This was the right decision.

06:28.889 --> 06:31.932
Hey, Chris, I'm super sorry
your sister is dead.

06:31.933 --> 06:34.393
Mwah.

06:34.394 --> 06:36.729
If there's anything
we can do to help you

06:36.730 --> 06:38.272
during your time of need...

06:38.273 --> 06:39.773
- Stamps.
- What?

06:39.774 --> 06:41.400
Stamps. I need stamps.

06:41.401 --> 06:43.742
Okay, you got it.

06:44.696 --> 06:47.948
Wow. Are girls coming on to me
because my sister died?

06:47.949 --> 06:49.909
Cool!

06:49.910 --> 06:52.411
<i>God, I wish it was Joe in that box.</i>

06:52.412 --> 06:53.871
I do, too, Bon.

06:53.872 --> 06:55.873
Oh. Did I say that out loud?

06:55.874 --> 06:58.292
No, but at this point,
I know what you're thinking.

06:58.293 --> 07:00.170
It'll be soon, babe.

07:03.715 --> 07:05.382
Unbelievable.

07:05.383 --> 07:07.217
There's hardly anyone here.

07:07.218 --> 07:09.053
Ugh. Well, that's it.

07:09.054 --> 07:12.043
I'm off to a new town
to start a new life.

07:12.044 --> 07:13.426
Ooh. Sorry.

07:13.427 --> 07:16.519
Don't you know what a rosary
on a doorknob means?!

07:30.659 --> 07:34.286
Siri, play "Kiss From a Rose" by Seal.

07:45.217 --> 07:47.466
I hope everyone enjoys tonight's dinner.

07:49.010 --> 07:51.095
It... it was Meg's favorite.

07:52.931 --> 07:55.140
There, there, Lois. Stop your crying.

07:55.141 --> 07:57.142
Stop it.

07:57.143 --> 07:59.103
Please stop. Stop.

07:59.104 --> 08:01.866
Stop it. Stop crying.

08:01.867 --> 08:03.357
Stop crying.

08:03.358 --> 08:05.943
Stop crying. Stop.

08:05.944 --> 08:07.628
Before we eat,

08:07.629 --> 08:10.073
would anyone like
to say something about Meg?

08:12.617 --> 08:16.389
Okay, I feel all of you
looking at me, so here goes.

08:16.390 --> 08:18.330
Meg, wherever you are,

08:18.331 --> 08:20.708
I hope that you're with Bubba,
and I want you to know

08:20.709 --> 08:22.626
that Lieutenant Dan is walking around...

08:22.627 --> 08:24.044
Is this from<i> Forrest Gump?</i>

08:24.045 --> 08:26.463
I miss you, Meg.

08:26.464 --> 08:27.965
Stop it, Brian.

08:27.966 --> 08:29.299
Stop your crying.

08:29.300 --> 08:30.843
Stop it.

08:30.844 --> 08:31.969
Please stop.

08:31.970 --> 08:34.054
Stop. Stop it.

08:34.055 --> 08:37.233
Stop crying. Stop crying.

08:37.234 --> 08:39.601
Stop crying. Stop.

08:39.602 --> 08:43.022
Stewie, is there anything
you'd like to say?

08:43.023 --> 08:46.191
Yeah. We're gonna save a lot
of money on toilet paper.

08:46.192 --> 08:47.985
Ever see her wipe?

08:47.986 --> 08:49.820
She'd wrap up both hands like oven mitts

08:49.821 --> 08:52.823
and act like she was cleaning
out a pot of burnt chili.

08:52.824 --> 08:56.535
Anyway, that's all
I care to say about Meg.

08:56.536 --> 08:58.746
Maybe we should just have
a moment of silence

08:58.747 --> 09:00.706
as we hear the guy down the street

09:00.707 --> 09:01.999
scream at his barking dog.

09:03.793 --> 09:05.878
Damn it, Rufus, shut up!

09:05.879 --> 09:07.504
Will you shut up?!

09:07.505 --> 09:10.425
Get in the house! Get in the house!

09:13.511 --> 09:17.598
♪ <i>This time things are gonna</i>
<i>work out fine</i> ♪

09:17.599 --> 09:20.893
♪ <i>This time will be better</i>
<i>than previous times</i> ♪

09:20.894 --> 09:23.687
♪ <i>This time is markedly different</i> ♪

09:23.688 --> 09:28.025
♪ <i>Than the times we had before</i> ♪

09:28.026 --> 09:32.029
♪ <i>This time is gonna be so much more!</i> ♪

09:34.074 --> 09:36.201
♪ <i>Or maybe it's not.</i> ♪

09:40.246 --> 09:42.748
Hi, new neighbor.

09:42.749 --> 09:44.041
I just thought I'd come by and see

09:44.042 --> 09:45.918
if I could borrow a cup of tampons.

09:45.919 --> 09:48.711
Sure. Just bring 'em back
when you're done. No rush.

09:48.712 --> 09:51.715
- Thanks. My name's not important.
- What's yours?

09:51.716 --> 09:54.093
Um... my name?

09:54.094 --> 09:55.512
My name is...

09:57.764 --> 09:59.389
Hallway.

09:59.390 --> 10:01.183
Natalie Hallway.

10:01.184 --> 10:02.808
Nice to meet you, Natalie.

10:02.809 --> 10:05.229
You want to join us on the roof
and sit under string lights?

10:05.230 --> 10:06.730
That sounds great!

10:06.731 --> 10:08.565
I'll bring my hemorrhoid donut
to sit on.

10:09.899 --> 10:11.568
Great joke, Natalie Hallway!

10:11.569 --> 10:13.570
Yes. It is a joke.

10:13.571 --> 10:15.739
Because Natalie Hallway doesn't need

10:15.740 --> 10:17.783
to sit on a hemorrhoid donut.

10:21.788 --> 10:24.836
To Natalie Hallway, our new friend.

10:26.084 --> 10:28.861
Natalie, sit down.
Tell us about yourself.

10:31.089 --> 10:32.798
<i>Yow...!</i>

10:32.799 --> 10:34.217
What a view!

10:38.638 --> 10:40.764
You know, Stewie, when Meg was little,

10:40.765 --> 10:44.060
we used to love to make
Christmas cookies together.

10:46.146 --> 10:48.814
Are... are those dongs?

10:48.815 --> 10:51.150
My God, from October to January

10:51.151 --> 10:52.776
I don't come up for air.

10:52.777 --> 10:55.612
All those families enjoying
their Christmas dongs.

10:55.613 --> 10:57.823
Could we get some of your
cookies for our wedding?

10:57.824 --> 10:59.449
Get out of here!
This is a family bakery!

10:59.450 --> 11:01.034
I'm a Christian!

11:01.035 --> 11:03.036
In the case of<i> Kent and Bradley</i>

11:03.037 --> 11:05.247
<i>v. Holiday Dongs,</i>

11:05.248 --> 11:08.876
the court rules that you
must give us the recipe.

11:08.877 --> 11:10.919
Oh!

11:10.920 --> 11:12.546
<i>Under court order, Stewie went on</i>

11:12.547 --> 11:14.673
<i>to make baked goods for the gay wedding.</i>

11:14.674 --> 11:16.967
<i>And because of that,
he did not get into heaven,</i>

11:16.968 --> 11:19.344
<i>just like they've always been saying.</i>

11:26.102 --> 11:27.853
Chris, be in my selfie!

11:27.854 --> 11:30.022
I want to make Meg's death about me.

11:31.232 --> 11:32.983
Hey, Chris, I couldn't help but notice

11:32.984 --> 11:34.401
how much attention you're getting.

11:34.402 --> 11:35.652
Want to high-five hug?

11:35.653 --> 11:38.155
Hell yes.

11:38.156 --> 11:39.823
Hang in there, brotha.

11:39.824 --> 11:42.159
I will,<i> brother.</i>

11:42.160 --> 11:44.912
Chris, here are the keys
to the drivers ed car

11:44.913 --> 11:46.747
to use anytime you want.

11:46.748 --> 11:49.708
- Wow, cool.
- See, everyone?

11:49.709 --> 11:52.836
If I were using the drivers ed
car for my real car,

11:52.837 --> 11:55.202
I wouldn't have given him the keys.

11:55.203 --> 11:56.743
That would be a psycho move.

11:56.744 --> 11:58.926
I wouldn't have a ride home.

11:58.927 --> 12:01.471
Chris, if you're heading home,
can I get a ride?

12:18.029 --> 12:19.321
- Yeah!
- Go, Natalie!

12:19.322 --> 12:20.697
Wow, Natalie Hallway,

12:20.698 --> 12:22.741
how did you get so good at bowling?

12:22.742 --> 12:24.117
Oh, I used to play a lot

12:24.118 --> 12:26.954
back in Qua... rea.

12:26.955 --> 12:28.733
Wow, you lived in Korea?

12:28.734 --> 12:30.040
Yep.

12:30.041 --> 12:31.875
When I was with the embassy.

12:31.876 --> 12:33.877
So was that before or after you were

12:33.878 --> 12:36.607
one of the first black women
to do math for NASA?

12:36.608 --> 12:37.714
Yes.

12:37.715 --> 12:41.510
Wow, your parents must be
so proud of you.

12:55.984 --> 12:57.484
Hey, Griffin, I heard you scored

12:57.485 --> 12:59.403
with the girls'
basketball team yesterday.

12:59.404 --> 13:02.072
Yep, 12 points and eight rebounds.

13:02.073 --> 13:03.740
Aw, Griffin, you're the man.

13:03.741 --> 13:05.492
I got an extra orange at lunch.

13:05.493 --> 13:07.412
- You want it?
- Yeah!

13:08.913 --> 13:11.081
Life is pretty sweet.

13:12.417 --> 13:13.667
Hello?

13:13.668 --> 13:14.668
Hey, Chris.

13:14.669 --> 13:15.919
Meg?!

13:15.920 --> 13:17.713
Are you alive?

13:17.714 --> 13:20.590
Yes. I'll explain everything.
Can you come meet me?

13:20.591 --> 13:22.926
Okay, still the cemetery?

13:22.927 --> 13:24.177
Alive?!

13:24.178 --> 13:25.929
Chris, you already know that part.

13:25.930 --> 13:27.180
Oh, right.

13:27.181 --> 13:29.933
So you suddenly got sick
of your new, great life?

13:29.934 --> 13:31.184
No, Chris.

13:31.185 --> 13:33.603
I can't believe I'm saying this, but...

13:33.604 --> 13:35.474
I missed Mom.

13:35.475 --> 13:37.079
I missed you.

13:37.080 --> 13:38.775
I missed the whole family.

13:38.776 --> 13:40.777
I'm glad you're alive,
but you should know

13:40.778 --> 13:42.279
things are different now.

13:42.280 --> 13:44.384
- Dad finally got a Peloton?
- Yeah.

13:44.385 --> 13:45.949
- Is he using it?
- No.

13:45.950 --> 13:47.284
He mumbled something about the Wi-Fi,

13:47.285 --> 13:49.119
then ate a whole chicken on the couch,

13:49.120 --> 13:51.371
- but there's something else.
- What is it?

13:51.372 --> 13:53.874
Let's talk about it in the van.

13:53.875 --> 13:54.875
Chris?!

13:54.876 --> 13:56.960
What are you doing?! Let me out!

13:56.961 --> 13:59.796
Sorry, Meg, but I can't
let you come home just yet.

13:59.797 --> 14:01.382
I'm too popular now.

14:03.968 --> 14:05.677
- What's the holdup?
- What?

14:05.678 --> 14:07.302
I slapped the van twice.

14:07.303 --> 14:10.015
Yeah, what was that?
I thought something flew into the van.

14:10.016 --> 14:11.892
No, that's, like, the universal signal

14:11.893 --> 14:13.310
for "move it out."

14:13.311 --> 14:14.853
I never heard that.

14:14.854 --> 14:16.313
And I drive vans all the time.

14:16.314 --> 14:18.398
Well, then how do you know
when it's time to head out?

14:18.399 --> 14:21.151
Somebody yells out
"okay" or "all right."

14:21.152 --> 14:22.986
Every so often it's "yep."

14:22.987 --> 14:25.655
Well, okay, you're good to go.

14:25.656 --> 14:28.158
All right.

14:28.159 --> 14:29.326
Ow! Ow!

14:29.327 --> 14:30.994
What are you doing?!

14:30.995 --> 14:32.913
Sorry, I got distracted by all this

14:32.914 --> 14:34.957
whappin' the side of the van business.

14:44.759 --> 14:48.063
Hello? Hello?

14:48.064 --> 14:50.013
Where is everyone?

14:50.014 --> 14:53.298
Damn it, Chris, I don't care
that you're popular now.

14:53.299 --> 14:55.060
Let me out of here!

14:55.061 --> 14:57.509
Well, at least I still have my music.

14:57.510 --> 15:00.190
Siri, play Seals and Croft.

15:00.191 --> 15:04.486
♪ <i>Darling if you want me to be...</i> ♪

15:06.239 --> 15:10.243
♪ <i>Get closer to me.</i> ♪

15:12.703 --> 15:15.080
Good morning, students.

15:15.081 --> 15:17.290
We are gathered here
for two reasons today.

15:17.291 --> 15:19.918
One, to mourn the loss of Meg Griffin.

15:19.919 --> 15:22.587
And two, to find the owner
of this X-Men water bottle

15:22.588 --> 15:24.780
someone left in wood shop...
Does anyone recognize it?

15:24.781 --> 15:28.218
- I'll take it!
- That's not what I asked. Anyone?

15:28.219 --> 15:29.970
I'm not gonna tell you
which character's on it,

15:29.971 --> 15:31.721
you have to be able
to tell<i> me</i> the character.

15:31.722 --> 15:33.056
Wolverine!

15:33.057 --> 15:34.599
- Are you guessing?
- Am I right?

15:34.600 --> 15:36.226
All right, we'll handle this after.

15:36.227 --> 15:39.646
But now, here to help you mourn,
an artist who specializes

15:39.647 --> 15:41.982
in sensitive music
to do finger stuff to,

15:41.983 --> 15:44.609
Mr. John Mayer!

15:44.610 --> 15:46.945
It's good to be here.
I love high school!

15:46.946 --> 15:49.739
Who are you? I was born in 2003!

15:49.740 --> 15:51.825
Then I'm probably your father.

15:51.826 --> 15:53.994
Ooh, pwned!

15:53.995 --> 15:57.289
Whoa, looks like the school
really is missing Meg.

15:57.290 --> 15:59.582
Chris, Brian, would you help Peter?

15:59.583 --> 16:02.962
He's one of those "has to be supported
by both elbows" mourners.

16:05.131 --> 16:08.536
I'm gonna need three seats
for my elbow supporters.

16:10.470 --> 16:12.345
Stewie, you look depressed.

16:12.346 --> 16:13.972
You still upset about Meg?

16:13.973 --> 16:15.980
No, it's just this gym is sad.

16:15.981 --> 16:18.477
If you haven't won
a championship since 1982,

16:18.478 --> 16:20.729
just take the banner down.

16:25.735 --> 16:27.652
Well, Meg,

16:27.653 --> 16:30.822
looks like you really
are dead this time.

16:30.823 --> 16:33.617
They say your life flashes
before your eyes when you die.

16:33.618 --> 16:36.161
I wonder what I'll see.

16:38.039 --> 16:39.247
Oh, yeah!

16:39.248 --> 16:40.373
Over!

16:40.374 --> 16:41.708
I'm a tomato.

16:43.461 --> 16:44.586
<i>I'm not in any of these!</i>

16:44.587 --> 16:45.795
Ladies and gentlemen,

16:45.796 --> 16:47.464
Mr. Conway Twitty.

16:47.465 --> 16:48.548
Oh, come on!

16:48.549 --> 16:50.133
I was in the<i> Kingsman</i> fight!

16:50.134 --> 16:51.426
That could've been in there.

16:51.427 --> 16:52.636
I can do stuff.

16:52.637 --> 16:54.937
I-I can be a part of a comedy team!

16:54.938 --> 16:57.181
Look, hey, Chris, who's on first?

16:57.182 --> 17:00.502
A baseball player.

17:00.503 --> 17:02.062
Well, that's it.

17:02.063 --> 17:03.897
I'm gonna show them.

17:03.898 --> 17:05.565
I'm gonna live.

17:05.566 --> 17:07.776
I'm getting out of here.

17:07.777 --> 17:10.070
Now let's see, if I whap my forehead

17:10.071 --> 17:12.072
against this cement floor enough times,

17:12.073 --> 17:14.658
I think I can create a blood luge

17:14.659 --> 17:16.535
to slide myself out on.

17:16.536 --> 17:18.995
This... this

17:18.996 --> 17:21.289
can be in the highlight

17:21.290 --> 17:23.209
video!

17:36.973 --> 17:39.891
Wow, thank you, John Mayer.
Wasn't he terrific?

17:39.892 --> 17:41.893
I think we can all agree
that John is entitled

17:41.894 --> 17:44.813
to take whichever student he
wishes home with him tonight.

17:46.482 --> 17:48.066
And finally, the Quiznos

17:48.067 --> 17:49.776
across the street has graciously

17:49.777 --> 17:51.945
taken out a full page ad in the yearbook

17:51.946 --> 17:54.448
that will feature
a dedication page to Meg.

17:56.492 --> 17:58.577
Quiznos, go ahead and stand up.

17:58.578 --> 18:01.087
Come on, in the back,
you guys have been great.

18:10.673 --> 18:12.090
Oh, my God, oh, my God, everyone!

18:12.091 --> 18:14.050
He's proposing right here!

18:14.051 --> 18:16.761
Right in front of everyone!
Oh, she's so lucky!

18:16.762 --> 18:18.179
Oh, my God!

18:19.932 --> 18:23.059
I'm alive! I'm alive!

18:24.228 --> 18:25.478
Meg!

18:25.479 --> 18:26.980
Those are dark-soled shoes.

18:26.981 --> 18:29.816
She's wearing dark-soled shoes
on the gym floor!

18:29.817 --> 18:32.068
Sneakers only in the gym, guys.

18:32.069 --> 18:33.690
Oh, my God, Meg!

18:33.691 --> 18:35.500
I'm so glad you're alive!

18:35.501 --> 18:36.989
What happened?

18:36.990 --> 18:39.076
He did this!

18:40.494 --> 18:42.621
Are you saying Chris saved your life?

18:42.622 --> 18:44.914
This calls for a celebration.

18:44.915 --> 18:46.916
All right, everyone throw confetti

18:46.917 --> 18:48.627
and ruin the janitor's weekend.

18:52.923 --> 18:55.091
Hey, I'm not gonna make it this weekend.

18:55.092 --> 18:58.094
Oh, but you're gonna miss
the big janitor dance!

18:58.095 --> 19:00.930
This is our last chance to get
laid before Janitor College!

19:00.931 --> 19:03.141
You think I don't know that?!

19:03.142 --> 19:06.561
No! Chris kidnapped me
so he could stay popular!

19:06.562 --> 19:09.718
What? Chris would never do that.

19:09.719 --> 19:10.857
Chris?

19:10.858 --> 19:12.652
It's true, Mom.

19:16.030 --> 19:18.156
I owe my sister an apology.

19:18.157 --> 19:20.530
I shouldn't have treated her
the way I did.

19:20.531 --> 19:22.452
And I think if Meg were here today,

19:22.453 --> 19:24.454
she'd be the first one to agree.

19:24.455 --> 19:25.789
I am here!

19:25.790 --> 19:27.123
I'm right here!

19:27.124 --> 19:29.111
Anyway, Meg, wherever you are,

19:29.112 --> 19:30.331
I'm sorry.

19:32.296 --> 19:35.048
Damn it, I'm giving a speech!
I want to tell you...

19:35.049 --> 19:38.275
Very loud chant! Very loud chant!

19:38.276 --> 19:40.512
Very loud chant! Very loud chant!

19:42.473 --> 19:44.974
Oh, my God, Meg,
I'm so glad you're back.

19:44.975 --> 19:46.940
We love you, honey.

19:46.941 --> 19:48.520
I love you, too, Mom.

19:48.521 --> 19:50.897
Yeah, Meg, I'm just really glad
this whole ordeal is over.

19:50.898 --> 19:52.691
<i>Glad this whole ordeal is what?</i>

19:52.692 --> 19:54.192
<i>Over.</i>

19:54.193 --> 19:56.400
Come on!

20:02.410 --> 20:04.446
I'm sorry I faked my own death, Mom.

20:04.447 --> 20:06.913
It's okay, Meg.
Actually, I should've known.

20:06.914 --> 20:09.082
Faking stuff is part of being a woman.

20:09.083 --> 20:10.861
- Really?
- Oh, yeah.

20:10.862 --> 20:12.375
Women fake a lot of things.

20:12.376 --> 20:14.879
You faked your death,
I fake orgasms and being

20:14.880 --> 20:17.674
impressed by my husband's
accomplishments at work.

20:17.675 --> 20:19.718
Hey, Lois, guess who got to erase

20:19.719 --> 20:21.678
the white board in a meeting today?

20:21.679 --> 20:23.012
Oh, my!

20:23.013 --> 20:25.098
I think someone's earned himself

20:25.099 --> 20:28.309
Mama Lois' famous egg salad, huh?

20:28.310 --> 20:29.352
Oh, yum!

20:29.353 --> 20:31.688
Oh, today just keeps getting
better and better!

20:31.689 --> 20:34.149
Dad, I thought you hated
Mom's egg salad.

20:34.150 --> 20:36.860
Chris, part of being a man
is faking things.

20:36.861 --> 20:40.196
Like orgasms or pretending
to like your wife's egg salad.

20:40.197 --> 20:43.325
And anyway, I give it to that
raccoon outside who likes me.

20:45.160 --> 20:46.876
I thought you hated that guy.

20:46.877 --> 20:49.706
Part of being a raccoon
is faking things.

20:49.707 --> 20:52.125
Like orgasms
or pretending to like people

20:52.126 --> 20:54.169
who give you egg salad.

20:54.170 --> 20:55.587
Oh, Peter!

20:55.588 --> 20:57.130
Oh, Lois!

20:57.131 --> 20:59.675
Oh, other raccoon!